<figure class="thread-media thread-media--linked"><a aria-label="Open the Eu Não Tô Nem Aí cover at full size" href="/assets/archive/music/coitado-do-proximo/2000-eu-nao-to-nem-ai/coitadodoproximo_00_eunaotonemai_2000_01_capa.jpg" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><img alt="Cover of Eu Não Tô Nem Aí, Coitado do Próximo’s second album, released in 2000." decoding="async" loading="lazy" src="/assets/archive/music/coitado-do-proximo/2000-eu-nao-to-nem-ai/coitadodoproximo_00_eunaotonemai_2000_01_capa.jpg" width="1254" height="1254"/></a><figcaption><strong>Eu Não Tô Nem Aí · 2000.</strong><span class="thread-media-note">Cover of Coitado do Próximo’s second album.</span><a class="thread-media-open" href="/assets/archive/music/coitado-do-proximo/2000-eu-nao-to-nem-ai/coitadodoproximo_00_eunaotonemai_2000_01_capa.jpg" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Open image at full size ↗</a></figcaption></figure><p>Second album in the original cycle, produced by <strong>Fábio Badi</strong>. Marcelo Minduim recorded drums.</p><p>Recorded between <strong>December 1999 and February 2000</strong> at <strong>Master Music</strong> and <strong>BHS</strong> studios, the CD edition contained <strong>eight tracks</strong>, combining original compositions and versions.</p><p>Released on CD in <strong>2000</strong>, the album opened new opportunities for media appearances and live performances.</p><div class="album-credits"><h3>Technical credits</h3><h4>Track listing</h4><ol><li><strong>A Enchente</strong> — Marcelo Minduim / Ricardo Bicária.</li><li><strong>Filhinho Coronel</strong> — Marcelo Minduim / Ricardo Bicária.</li><li><strong>Estava Comigo</strong> — Marcelo Minduim.</li><li><strong>Mulher SP</strong> — Marcelo Minduim.</li><li><strong>Eu Não Tô Nem Aí</strong> — Fat Mike (NOFX); version: Marcelo Minduim.</li><li><strong>Você Merece</strong> — Marcelo Minduim.</li><li><strong>Ninguém Imaginava</strong>.</li><li><strong>Ciúmes</strong> — version of Ultraje a Rigor.</li></ol><h4>Personnel</h4><ul><li><strong>Vocals:</strong> Mario Joe.</li><li><strong>Guitars:</strong> Ricardo Bicária and Fábio Badi.</li><li><strong>Bass:</strong> Bel.</li><li><strong>Drums:</strong> Marcelo Minduim.</li><li><strong>Keyboards:</strong> Alexandre Totti.</li></ul><h4>Special guests</h4><p><strong>“Você Merece”:</strong> trumpet — Lucas Cavalcanti; saxophone — Alexandre Borges; trombone — Ricardo Guedes.</p><h4>Recording and production</h4><ul><li><strong>Recording:</strong> Estúdio Master Music and Estúdio BHS — December 1999 to February 2000.</li><li><strong>Drum mixing:</strong> Paulo Anhaia — Estúdio Midas.</li><li><strong>Mixing:</strong> Fábio Badi.</li><li><strong>Production:</strong> Fábio Badi.</li><li><strong>Mastering:</strong> Rodrigo Castanho — Estúdio Midas.</li></ul><h4>Studios by session</h4><ul><li><strong>Estúdio Master Music:</strong> drums, vocals, backing vocals, choirs, brass and keyboards.</li><li><strong>Estúdio Midas:</strong> drum mixing — Paulo Anhaia.</li><li><strong>Estúdio BHS:</strong> guitars, bass and keyboards.</li></ul></div><div class="video-library audio-library album-audio-library" aria-label="Preserved audio" aria-labelledby="music-album-2000-audio-title">
